From: dsanke <dsanke1997@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: release HW_RRO sessions on station removal

An RX BlockAck stop may race with station teardown or never be observed for
every TID.  The firmware-assigned session IDs persisted in 0016 must
then be released when the station link is removed; otherwise the NPU can
retain the same stale per-WCID RRO context that poisons WCID
reuse after reconnect.

Consume each ID atomically and issue the existing RRO delete command before
the WTBL/WCID state is detached.  Normal RX BA stop has already cleared its
ID, so this path does not duplicate releases.

Signed-off-by: dsanke <dsanke1997@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/main.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1192,8 +1192,25 @@ mt7996_mac_sta_init_link(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void
+mt7996_sta_release_rro_sessions(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
+				struct mt7996_sta_link *msta_link)
+{
+	int tid;
+
+	if (!mt7996_has_hwrro(dev))
+		return;
+
+	for (tid = 0; tid < IEEE80211_NUM_TIDS; tid++) {
+		u16 session_id = xchg(&msta_link->rro_id[tid], 0);
+
+		if (session_id)
+			mt7996_mcu_wed_rro_reset_sessions(dev, session_id);
+	}
+}
+
 void mt7996_mac_sta_remove_link(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
 				struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
 				unsigned int link_id, bool flush)
 {
 	struct mt7996_sta *msta = (struct mt7996_sta *)sta->drv_priv;
@@ -1203,6 +1222,8 @@ void mt7996_mac_sta_remove_link(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
 	if (!msta_link)
 		return;
 
+	mt7996_sta_release_rro_sessions(dev, msta_link);
+
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->mt76.sta_poll_lock);
 	if (!list_empty(&msta_link->wcid.poll_list))
 		list_del_init(&msta_link->wcid.poll_list);
